practACE - 1.5 Sprint Algorithm
1. Overview & Objective
The practACE 1.5 Sprint Algorithm is designed to optimize revision schedules for competitive/professional exam preparations (FR, AFM, Audit, DT, IDT, IBS) during the critical 1.5-day exam sprint window. It dynamically calculates available study time, allocates proportionate target time based on subject categories (ABC Analysis), and dynamically re-balances schedules when targets are delayed or skipped.
2. Sprint Schedule Boundaries
2.1 Start Time Configuration
* FR: 5 days prior to Exam Date (e.g., if FR exam is Nov 2, start on Oct 29).
* AFM, Audit, DT, IDT, IBS: 7:00 PM on the day of the previous exam.
2.2 End Time Configuration
* Standard Target End Time: 9:30 AM on Exam Date.
* Maximum Flexible End Time: Up to 12:30 PM on Exam Date (includes breaks).
3. Time Allocation Framework
3.1 Available Time Metrics
* Total Available Time: (Start Time to 9:30 AM End Time) minus:
   * 6 hours sleep time per day transition.
   * 1 hour routine allowance on Start Day and Exam Day.
   * 2 hours routine allowance on full study days.
* Max Available Time: Total Available Time + 3 Flexible Hours (extending target end time from 9:30 AM to 12:30 PM).
3.2 Proportionate Allocation Algorithm
* Order of Priority: Sort revision targets using standard ABC Category Analysis.
* Historical Baseline: Retrieve average completion time for each target from revision report logs.
* Weight Calculation: Compute normalized weights for each chapter based on its category (A, B, C) and baseline historical time (Sum of all chapter weights = 1.0).
* Time Assignment: Multiply each chapter weight by the Total Available Time.
4. Dynamic Re-Balancing & Flexible Time Rules
When real-time completion delays occur relative to the planned Max Proportionate Time, the system activates dynamic adjustment phases in sequential order:
* Priority Level 1 (Extension): Extend target completion time dynamically up to 12:30 PM (Max Available Time) while preserving original chapter weights.
* Priority Level 2 (Uniform Reduction): If Max Available Time (12:30 PM limit) is breached, apply an equal proportionate time reduction across all remaining chapters based on historical averages.
* Priority Level 3 (Category Minimum Floor Limits):
   * Category A Floor: Must retain at least 60% (absolute lower limit: 40%) of original allocated time.
   * Category B Floor: Must retain at least 30% (absolute lower limit: 20%) of original allocated time.
   * Category C Floor: Allocate remaining balance, establishing a minimum threshold per chapter of 25% (absolute lower limit: 10%–15%) of baseline time.
5. System Constraints & User Overrides
* Coverage Optimization Constraint: The total number of skipped chapters must be minimized. The system must maximize total chapter coverage prior to dropping targets.
* Manual User Overrides: Allow users to manually toggle/skip specific chapters. Skipped chapters are excluded from dynamic time redistribution calculations.